       fhir:display [ fhir:v "language" ] ;
       fhir:target ( [
         fhir:code [ fhir:v "Basic.language" ] ;
         fhir:display [ fhir:v "Basic.language" ] ;
         fhir:equivalence [ fhir:v "equivalent" ] ;
         fhir:comment [ fhir:v "Element matches Basic element path `Basic.language` (`Resource.language`), use that element instead.\nElement `NutritionIntake.language` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `NutritionIntake` is not mapped.\nElement `NutritionIntake.language` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).\nLanguage is provided to support indexing and accessibility (typically, services such as text to speech use the language tag). The html language tag in the narrative applies  to the narrative. The language tag on the resource may be used to specify the language of other presentations generated from the data in the resource. Not all the content has to be in the base language. The Resource.language should not be assumed to apply to the narrative automatically. If a language is specified, it should it also be specified on the div element in the html (see rules in HTML5 for information about the relationship between xml:lang and the html lang attribute)." ]
       ] )
     ] [
       fhir:code [ fhir:v "NutritionIntake.text" ] ;
       fhir:display [ fhir:v "text" ] ;
       fhir:target ( [
         fhir:code [ fhir:v "Basic.text" ] ;
         fhir:display [ fhir:v "Basic.text" ] ;
         fhir:equivalence [ fhir:v "equivalent" ] ;
         fhir:comment [ fhir:v "Element matches Basic element path `Basic.text` (`DomainResource.text`), use that element instead.\nElement `NutritionIntake.text` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `NutritionIntake` is not mapped.\nElement `NutritionIntake.text` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).\nContained resources do not have a narrative. Resources that are not contained SHOULD have a narrative. In some cases, a resource may only have text with little or no additional discrete data (as long as all minOccurs=1 elements are satisfied).  This may be necessary for data from legacy systems where information is captured as a \"text blob\" or where text is additionally entered raw or narrated and encoded information is added later." ]
       ] )
     ] [
       fhir:code [ fhir:v "NutritionIntake.contained" ] ;
